<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Mutual reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Mutual reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Mutual Life Insurance Co has disclosed its restructured loans</p>
<p>(in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	     13.0	    25.84</p>
<p>  Bad loans			 20.04		2.9</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	   2.34	     2.23</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	   35.38	    30.96</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more.</p>
</text>
